<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Overrides the SDK's splash drawable, which spells out "loading…" and so
    says the same thing for every tool built with it. An app resource wins over
    a library one of the same name, which is the only way in: the generated
    manifest hardcodes the splash theme and a hand-written manifest is refused.

    The mark is Home Assistant's own logomark, taken unaltered from their brand
    assets (logo/home-assistant-logo.zip, monochrome variant) — only recoloured
    to the grey this app already uses for secondary content, so the splash
    belongs to the same two-ink palette as everything after it.

    Sized for the splash screen's safe area rather than the viewport: Android
    fits the icon inside a circle well short of the drawable's edges, and this
    mark runs corner to corner in its own box, so it is scaled into the middle
    and centred rather than trusting the full 288.
-->
